14. Create TestNG XML File  
Now we will use a TestNG XML file to select groups.  Right-click the project:  
TestNG → Convert to TestNG  
If this option is available, select it.  
Alternatively:  
File → New → Other → TestNG → TestNG Class  
Create: 
testng.xml  
A simple XML file can be:  
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>  
  
<!DOCTYPE suite SYSTEM  
"https://testng.org/testng-1.0.dtd">  
  
<suite name="TestNG Suite">  
  
    <test name="Smoke Tests">  
  
        <groups>  
            <run>  
                <include name="Smoke"/>  
            </run>  
        </groups>  
  
        <classes>  
            <class name="tests.SauceDemoTest"/>  
        </classes>  
  
    </test>  
 </suite> 
   
15. Run Only Smoke Tests  
Right-click:  
testng.xml  
Select:  
Run As → TestNG Suite  Only these tests will execute:  
Login Test  
Title Test  
The Regression test will not execute.  
   
